  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic metrics prove pipeline mechanics, not real-ore accuracy.",
    "Public metrics use dataset-provided polygons whose human-review status is unverified; they are not a hardware or production acceptance result.",
    "The S1 scene state has no 3-D geometry, volume, mass, material or grade fields.",
    "No depth, TF, DDS, device or motion path is exercised by S1.",
    "Scores are heuristic and uncalibrated; operating-point precision/recall are not guarantees.",
    "Latency is single-process CPU on 640x480 synthetic and 2592x1944 public images; no GPU or Pi 5 measurement."
  ],
  "negative_findings": [
    "Initial empty-scene test produced 17-18 false instances per featureless belt; fixed with an Otsu class-contrast gate and minimum foreground fraction.",
    "The classical baseline under-segments dense piles: synthetic dense AP50 is lower than sparse, and public 40-70mm predicts ~360 stones per image versus ~1150 annotated stones.",
    "Lab border-colour foreground and local-maxima seeds were tested and rejected on the synthetic tuning set (lower AP50 than Otsu-gray + global peaks).",
    "The public transport subset contains no ore annotations (COCO person_keypoints template), so it was not used for accuracy."
  ],
